        "original_id": "3fb94977-aa6d-5216-b369-a9d01216a854",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 1996 PGA Championship, 2000 PGA Championship\n- Places: Valhalla Golf Club, Louisville, Kentucky\n- People: Mark Brooks, Kenny Perry, Tiger Woods, Bob May\n\nFacts:\n- The 1996 PGA Championship was the 78th PGA Championship and was held August 8–11 at Valhalla Golf Club in Louisville, Kentucky.\n- Mark Brooks won the 1996 PGA Championship, his only major championship, with a birdie on the first hole of a sudden-death playoff against Kentucky native Kenny Perry.\n- The 2000 PGA Championship was the 82nd PGA Championship and was held August 17–20 at Valhalla Golf Club in Louisville, Kentucky.\n- Tiger Woods won the 2000 PGA Championship, his second straight PGA Championship and fifth major, in a three-hole playoff over Bob May.",
